@{ ViewData["Title"] = "Ingestion lab"; ViewData["Page"] = "telemetry"; }
<div class="page-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">CONTROLLED INPUT / VISIBLE RESULTS</span><h1>Put the gateway to work.</h1><p>Submit a typed reading or compare the latest output of two smart meters.</p></div></div>
<div class="dashboard-grid"><section class="panel form-panel"><span class="eyebrow">01 / SINGLE READING</span><h2>Send a telemetry packet</h2><p class="muted">Use a newly registered sensor for manual input. Seeded devices are also updated by the simulator.</p><form id="ingest-form"><label for="ingest-id">Sensor identifier<input id="ingest-id" required value="" placeholder="Your registered device ID" maxlength="64" /></label><label for="ingest-kind">Payload type<select id="ingest-kind"><option value="float">Float · temperature °C</option><option value="integer">Integer · power W</option><option value="boolean">Boolean · valve state</option></select></label><label for="ingest-value">Value<input id="ingest-value" required placeholder="e.g. 24.5, 420 or true" /></label><label for="ingest-sequence">Sequence number<input id="ingest-sequence" type="number" min="0" max="9007199254740991" value="1" required /><small>Must increase with every accepted packet for this sensor.</small></label><button class="button primary">Transmit packet ↗</button></form><pre id="ingest-result" class="result">The gateway response will appear here.</pre></section><section class="panel form-panel"><span class="eyebrow">02 / POWER COMPARISON</span><h2>One sum. Two perspectives.</h2><p class="muted">Compare integer watt readings from two registered power meters. Results include each sample's timestamp.</p><form id="power-form"><label for="power-left">Left meter<input id="power-left" required value="SX-0002" /></label><label for="power-right">Right meter<input id="power-right" required value="SX-0005" /></label><button class="button primary">Compare meters ↗</button></form><div id="power-result" class="power-result"><span class="muted">Select two meters to inspect their combined load and signed difference.</span></div><div class="annotation">A negative delta means the right meter is drawing more power. This demonstration uses the latest reading from each meter; timestamps may differ.</div></section></div>
